  "question": {
    ":question/id": "61aa0eda-a6ca-5084-8edb-f4a15105c84b",
    ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{3}}}-5$ for $t>0$.\n\n{{selection}}",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{3}}}-5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(-\\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}-5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -\\int t^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-5\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -\\frac{t^{-\\frac{3}{2}+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}-5\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}-5t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
